course: everyday
lesson: 517
title: The parent who left, and a new partner
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: On his tenth birthday Corey sits by the phone all afternoon, cake untouched. Dad doesn't call. Mum puts her arm round him: «His loss, love.» Corey is gutted (very, very disappointed). Mum doesn't pretend Dad is busy; she tells him the truth: «This is about your dad, not about you. You did nothing wrong.» Dad doesn't ring that year either. Uncle Kev takes him bowling instead, and Corey wins, and it still doesn't fix the ache. When a parent leaves and doesn't keep in touch, it is never the child's fault.
explain: Hallie's mom lives in Arizona and calls only at Christmas. Hallie holds the phone and can't think of a single thing to say. «Uh... I got a scooter.» Afterwards Grandpa ruffles her hair: «Bummer of a call, kiddo? Back in my day we just talked about the weather.» («Bummer» is an old word for a shame.) A parent you hardly see can feel like a stranger, and awkward is normal. Daisy scrolls Instagram and sees Dad's new family: two little kids at the beach, Dad grinning. She feels replaced. Her big cousin says, «Lowkey that's rough» (lowkey = a bit, quietly), «but you're not replaced, you're his first.» Mum asks Dad to call more. He calls twice, then less again.
explain: New partners can be lovely, and that can feel complicated. Gareth makes Leon pancakes every Saturday and sits through his fractions without sighing. Leon starts to like him, then feels guilty, as if he's betraying Dad. Nan says, «Your heart's not a cake, pet. You don't run out of slices.» Sasha's dad's girlfriend paints her nails and takes her shopping. Sasha's friend says, «Okay, she's giving fairy godmother» («it's giving» means it looks like, it has the vibe of). But when Sasha gets home, Mom goes quiet. Sasha says, «I had fun, but you're my mom.» Mom hugs her: «You're allowed to have fun, honey.»
explain: Not every new partner gets it right. Mum's boyfriend Craig tells Zane, «My house, my rules, mate.» Zane snaps, «It's Mum's house.» He tells Mum, and Mum and Craig agree that Mum makes the big rules for now. When Riley's mum's partner moves in with his son Kai, Riley's bedroom goes to Kai and Riley gets the box room. He feels pushed out and says so. They paint the box room the colour he picks, dark green, and Kai helps. Riley still misses his old room, and that's allowed.
explain: Broken promises hurt in a special way. Dad promises Paige the zoo on Saturday. She waits on the doorstep in her coat for two hours; he doesn't show and doesn't text. She cries, and Mum lets her; next time Dad promises something, Mum keeps a plan B ready, just in case. At Mum's wedding Sky is a bridesmaid in a lilac dress. She smiles in every photo, then cries in the loo, happy and sad at once. Jordan's dad comes back for a month, all takeaways and football, then is gone again. The third time, Jordan doesn't get excited at all. «I don't get my hopes up no more.» His teacher says feeling numb can be the heart protecting itself, and that talking to a trusted adult helps, even when the ending isn't happy.
fact: When a parent leaves or doesn't keep in touch, it is never the child's fault.
fact: Feeling gutted, angry or numb when a parent lets you down is normal.
fact: A phone call with a parent you rarely see can feel awkward, and that is okay.
fact: Seeing a parent's new family can make a child feel replaced, but new children don't replace the first ones.
fact: Liking a parent's new partner does not betray your other parent; love doesn't run out.
fact: A child can enjoy time with a new partner and still be loyal to both parents.
fact: A new partner shouldn't take over the rules straight away; the parent makes the big rules.
fact: When a new family moves in, space should be shared fairly, and a child can say if they feel pushed out.
fact: Broken promises hurt, and it is fine to cry and to tell a trusted adult.
fact: Big days like a parent's wedding can feel happy and sad at the same time.
fact: A parent who keeps coming and going can make a child stop hoping; talking to a trusted adult helps.
fact: «Gutted» means very disappointed, «bummer» is an old word for a shame, «lowkey» means a bit or quietly, and «it's giving» means it looks like.
exercise: Corey's dad doesn't call on his birthday. Whose fault is it? | Not Corey's | Corey's, for not ringing Dad himself first | Mum's, for not reminding his dad about it | Corey's, for being cross with Dad last year
exercise: What does «gutted» mean? | Very disappointed | Very hungry after skipping tea | A bit bored | Really pleased
exercise: How did Mum help Corey? | She told him the truth: it was about Dad, not him | She said Dad was just very busy and would ring soon | She rang Dad and shouted at him until he called | She told Corey to forget he ever had a dad at all
exercise: Hallie's mom calls once a year and Hallie can't think what to say. What's true? | Feeling awkward is normal | She must have something wrong with her | She should hang up straight away | She should never answer the phone again
exercise: Grandpa says, «Bummer of a call, kiddo?» What does «bummer» mean? | A shame, a let-down | A funny joke | A long, cosy chat about everything | A wrong number
exercise: Daisy sees Dad's new family on Instagram and feels replaced. What's true? | New children don't replace her; she's his first | Her dad loves the new kids more, because they're younger | She should follow them and post nasty comments back | She is replaced now and should forget about her dad
exercise: Did Dad keep calling Daisy more? | Twice, then less again | Yes, every day from then on | No, never once | He moved back home
exercise: Leon likes Gareth and feels guilty. What did Nan mean by «your heart's not a cake»? | You can love new people without taking love away from Dad | Leon should stop eating so much cake on Saturdays | Gareth's pancakes are healthier than cake | Leon has to choose one dad and stick with him
exercise: «She's giving fairy godmother.» What does «it's giving» mean? | It looks like, it has the vibe of | She is giving away presents | She is a real fairy | It's a gift shop on the high street
exercise: Sasha had fun with Dad's girlfriend and Mom went quiet. What did Sasha say? | «I had fun, but you're my mom» | «She's nicer than you, Mom» | «I'm moving in with them now» | Nothing, she hid the nail polish
exercise: «My house, my rules, mate,» says Craig. What did Zane do? | Told Mum, who said she'd make the big rules | Packed a bag and ran away to his mate's house | Did everything Craig said without a word | Shouted at Craig every day until he left
exercise: Riley's room went to Kai. What made it a bit fairer? | Riley picked the colour for the box room | Kai was sent to live somewhere else | Riley got Mum's bedroom instead of the box room | Kai had to pay rent to Riley every single week
exercise: Dad promised Paige the zoo and didn't show. What is right? | It's fine to be upset and to tell a trusted adult | She should pretend she never wanted to go anyway | She must have done something to make him stay away | She should wait on the doorstep until he turns up
exercise: Sky smiled in the wedding photos and cried later. Why? | Big days can feel happy and sad at once | She hated the lilac dress | She was only pretending to be happy | She had lost her shoes somewhere in the hotel
exercise: Jordan's dad keeps coming and going. Why did Jordan stop getting excited? | To protect himself from being let down again | Because he doesn't like takeaways or football | Because his dad asked him not to get excited | Because he forgot who his dad was
test: «if my dad really loved me he'd ring, so it's my fault innit». Right? | No, it's about Dad, never the child | Yes, kids make parents stop calling | Yes, if you were naughty that year | No, it's Mum's fault for him leaving
test: Daisy's mate: «ur dad's got new kids so he's done with u, deal with it». What's true? | He hasn't replaced her; the hurt is real but she's still his child | She should accept that she has been replaced for good | It is true, as dads only keep the youngest children | She must stop being sad, because new babies are normal
test: Leon: «if I like Gareth, Dad'll think I've swapped him». What would a wise grown-up say? | You can like Gareth and still love Dad | You have to pick one of them | Never tell anyone you like Gareth | Stop liking Gareth, just to be on the safe side
test: What would most likely happen if Craig kept making new rules without Mum? | More rows, and Zane would feel even worse | Zane would soon love the rules and Craig | Mum would hand the whole house to Craig | Nothing, new partners always make the rules
test: Riley: «it's well unfair, Kai got my room!!» Mum still can't give it back. What is a fair thing she can do? | Listen, and let Riley make the new room his own | Tell him to stop moaning, it's only a bedroom | Give Riley money so he stops going on about it | Pretend she didn't hear and change the subject
test: Paige's dad doesn't show for the zoo. Next week he promises the cinema. What would most likely help Paige? | Mum stays ready with a plan B, just in case | Waiting on the doorstep again, all day if needed | Telling herself she must stop wanting things | Ringing him every five minutes on Saturday morning
test: In a film, the new stepmum is a wicked witch. What's more real? | Many new partners are kind, some get it wrong | All stepmums are wicked, like in the stories | Every new partner is perfect from day one | New partners never want to meet the kids
test: Jordan: «don't care if he comes back, whatever». Does he really not care? | Probably he cares, and numb is protecting him | No, he has truly forgotten all about his dad | Yes, kids stop caring after a month apart | No, he only cares about the takeaways
test: ★★★ Jordan's dad came back in January, left in February, came back in June, left in July, came back in October. How many times has he come back this year so far? | 3 | 2 | 5 | 4
test: ★★★ Corey says, «Dad didn't ring on my 9th or my 10th, but he rang at Christmas between them.» How many of those three days did Dad ring? | 1 | 2 | 3 | 0
test: Sky's cousin: «u cried at the wedding?? so u hate ur stepdad». What's true? | Big days can bring happy and sad tears | Crying always means you hate someone | Bridesmaids are not allowed to cry | Sky must have been ill that day and kept it quiet
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the responsibility for a parent's failure to maintain contact? | The failure rests with the parent and never with the child | The failure arises where a child neglects to telephone | The failure is the remaining parent's in every case | The failure is attributable to the child's past conduct
exam: Identify the principal reason a child may cease to anticipate the return of a parent who repeatedly departs. | To protect himself from repeated disappointment | Because the child has wholly forgotten the parent | Because the parent has instructed the child to do so | Because the child no longer wishes to receive takeaways
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning affection for a parent's new partner. | It does not diminish, nor betray, the love owed to the other parent | It necessarily replaces the love formerly felt for the other parent | It must be concealed from all members of the family indefinitely | It is permissible only after the elapse of one complete year
exam: Given that a new partner seeks to impose rules within the parent's household, ascertain the arrangement established in the lesson. | The parent determines the principal rules for the present | The new partner determines all rules from the first day | The child determines the rules by majority vote | No rules whatsoever are to be applied in the household
